## Discovering Object Properties

One command I'll continue using is:

```powershell
Get-Service | Get-Member
```

This displays all the properties and methods available on the objects returned by `Get-Service`.

You can also inspect all properties of a single object:

```powershell
Get-Service | Select-Object -First 1 *
```

---

## Properties Commonly Used for Filtering

### Services

```powershell
Get-Service
```

Useful properties:

* `Name`
* `DisplayName`
* `Status`
* `ServiceType`

### Processes

```powershell
Get-Process
```

Useful properties:

* `Name`
* `Id`
* `CPU`
* `Handles`
* `WorkingSet`

### Local Users

```powershell
Get-LocalUser
```

Useful properties:

* `Name`
* `Enabled`
* `Description`
* `SID`

### Files and Directories

```powershell
Get-ChildItem
```

Useful properties:

* `Name`
* `Length`
* `Extension`
* `CreationTime`

